# 🌐 TryHackMe – Extending Your Network

## 📌 Overview
This room explores how computer networks can be expanded to connect multiple devices and networks. It covers networking concepts, devices, and technologies that help extend network connectivity beyond a single local network.

## 🎯 What I Learned

- **Network Devices:** Understanding the roles of routers, switches, and access points.
- **Routing:** Learning how data travels between different networks.
- **Subnetting:** Understanding how networks can be divided into smaller subnets.
- **VLANs:** Learning how Virtual LANs segment networks logically.
- **Wireless Networking:** Exploring how wireless devices connect to existing networks.
- **Network Expansion:** Understanding how multiple networks can communicate and share resources.

## 🔍 Key Concepts

| Concept | Description |
|---|---|
| Router | Connects different networks |
| Switch | Connects devices within a LAN |
| Access Point | Provides wireless network connectivity |
| VLAN | Creates logical network segments |
| Subnetting | Divides a network into smaller networks |
| Routing | Forwards packets between networks |
| LAN | Local Area Network |
| WAN | Wide Area Network |

## 🛠️ Skills Practiced
- Networking Fundamentals
- Network Architecture
- Routing and Switching
- Subnetting
- VLAN Configuration Concepts
- Wireless Networking
- Network Segmentation
- Network Troubleshooting

